{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1102306-gifts-in-w20","id":1102306,"title":"Gifts in W20","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-06-10T11:19:13-07:00","id":1102306,"title":"Gifts in W20","content":"I was rereading the W20 core, and under learning gifts I didn't see it state that rank 4 and 5 gifts are now the domain of specifically that breed/auspice/tribe/fera type....is it posted somewhere else in W20 or do people think this is a rule that was reversed with the new edition?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","name":"CeltSPZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"835"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-10T11:43:42-07:00","id":1102316,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CeltSPZ</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1102306-gifts-in-w20#post1102306\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was rereading the W20 core, and under learning gifts I didn't see it state that rank 4 and 5 gifts are now the domain of specifically that breed/auspice/tribe/fera type....is it posted somewhere else in W20 or do people think this is a rule that was reversed with the new edition?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't remember it being mentioned specifically (which doesn't mean it isn't there) but I would assume it's an oversight.<br /> <br /> Then again, I fall back on knowledge of previous editions whenever I'm unsure of something in W20 and don't feel like taking the time to look it up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-10T19:48:55-07:00","id":1102414,"title":"","content":"I don't recall any older rules saying that Rank 4 and 5 Gifts couldn't be learned out of splat... so W20 not saying it just seemed like business as usual to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-10T21:09:19-07:00","id":1102431,"title":"","content":"I agree, though you are limited to the third level when learning Gifts from another species of Fera.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-10T23:01:00-07:00","id":1102441,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1102306-gifts-in-w20?p=1102431#post1102431\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I agree, though you are limited to the third level when learning Gifts from another species of Fera.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the Fera type is the rule he/she is thinking of.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-11T08:10:49-07:00","id":1102511,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1102306-gifts-in-w20?p=1102441#post1102441\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the Fera type is the rule he/she is thinking of.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It was, granted there are some gifts that I can't help but think thematically wouldn't be too bad if another fera breed ended up with access to them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","name":"CeltSPZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"835"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-11T13:07:23-07:00","id":1102590,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CeltSPZ</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1102306-gifts-in-w20?p=1102511#post1102511\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It was, granted there are some gifts that I can't help but think thematically wouldn't be too bad if another fera breed ended up with access to them.</div> </div> </div> </div>And some Gifts are the same between Fera at those levels. So either the writers contradict their own rule (which happens all the time in WoD) or 2 different Fera were taught different Gifts that use the same system. <br /> <br /> Either way, for my games, if a Gift is thematically appropriate for a Fera/Breed/Auspice/Tribe then I don't see why it shouldn't be available. Especially since Garou get a lot more Gifts written than any other Fera. The Corax Gift list for example are kind of pathetic and could use a dozen or 2 more.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-11T13:24:29-07:00","id":1102595,"title":"","content":"I always interpreted it as could couldn't buy other Fera Gifts at Rank 4+ because those increasingly represent the unique powers of those Fera, except the Garou Gift lists which everyone has access to (being huge and rarely dealing in things like needing wings, being cold blooded, or using blood as a power source). But really noting is harmed if you break this when it feels appropriate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-18T02:21:44-07:00","id":1105007,"title":"","content":"I could have sworn I came across a mention in a 20th anniversary book somewhere explaining cross-fera gifts with the usual restrictions (nothing that depends on particular anatomy, nothing you could already learn at a different rank, etc), but without the cap at rank 3. I was just looking for it the other day though, and I can't seem to find it. I know I'm not thinking of the gifts section of the main W20 book, because that doesn't mention the special cross-fera considerations. Personally I'm already inclined to allow cross-list gift learning pretty freely* (as long as it meets those other restrictions, pay your higher XP cost and be done with it), but if the rule was officially updated in any way I'd like to know where it was.<br /> <br /> *I was actually even thinking of a homebrew merit for this, something like: Choose one gift list (breed/tribe/auspice/fera/regional variant/etc). Whether due to social connections or an unusual supernatural affinity, you can learn these gifts more easily. You can petition teachers (spirit or shapechanger) as easily as you do for your own base lists, and pay a reduced cost of gift rank x4. Optional extra note: If you choose a cross-fera list and the rank 3 cap is in effect, this merit allows you to learn rank 4/5 gifts at the full cross-list cost (rank x5). The other restrictions on cross-fera gifts still apply.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13544-impeesa","name":"Impeesa","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"21"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}